^ ","^17","finance"],536876399]],["^15",[1115,"^H",1101,536876399]],["^15",[1115,"^;","~u6673cbeb-7921-4e82-b72d-4d09072e0f53",536876399]],["^15",[1116,"^Q","tags:: finance\n\n",536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^O","^16",536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^1B",["^18",[]],536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^F",672,536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^X",672,536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^V",672,536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^U",672,536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^U",1101,536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^:",true,536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^?",["^ ","^17",["^18",["finance"]]],536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^J",["^17"],536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^4",["^ ","^17","finance"],536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^H",1101,536876402]],["^15",[1116,"^;","~u6673cbeb-ca50-48f1-ad61-c13d6683a714",536876402]],["^15",[1120,"^12",2,536876416]],["^15",[1121,"^3","tags:: finance\n\n- Implements the nation's ((667483a2-4985-4618-a070-1de207083ed8))\n\t- Rather than try to regulate the quantity of credit it attempts to influence the **price of credit** using its monetary policy tools\n\t- Every commercial bank may need to borrow reserves from either the central bank or other commercial banks\n\t- Banks access reserves indirectly via the interbank or wholesale market by selling or lending government securities (gilts)\n\t- Banks lend reserves to each other at the market rate of interest. The closer the market rate of interest is to the ((6670986e-abc1-406d-9c06-4a5cd5720586)) the more effectively changes in the ((6670986e-abc1-406d-9c06-4a5cd5720586)) will carry through and the more reliably monetary policy is implemented\n\t- The central bank cannot directly determine the market rate of interest in the interbank market, but it can affect the market rate of interest by lending and borrowing reserves itself on this market to try and keep this rate close to the policy rate. These loans are conducted via repurchasing agreements (repos) and other open-market operations or through providing ‘standing facilities’.\n\t- Since the rate charged on the loans is the Monetary Policy Committee’s policy rate, and the demand for reserves is met by the supply from the central bank, traded rates in the money market tend to be close to the policy rate\n\t- If the interbank rate is significantly above the policy rate the central bank can make additional loans to the banks collateralised by goverment securities, or it can engage in outright asset purchases\n\t-\n- Banks are required to hold a certain amount of ((6665782c-8bea-467c-8657-7183e047c130)) with the central bank\n\t- TODO define what this \"certain amount\" is\n\t- Financial institutions may have a surplus or deficit of ((6665782c-8bea-467c-8657-7183e047c130)) so they borrow and lend to each other in this market\n\t- The majority of these loans are made overnight it is also know as the overnight market\n- ((667483a2-4985-4618-a070-1de207083ed8)) tools\n\t- Open Market Operations (OMO)\n\t\t- The primary goal is to supply a sufficient quantity of reserves\n\t\t- Nowadays, only secured loans and ((6674a921-d46f-4adb-9b5d-a99ba47d7fa7)) are used in OMO rather than goverment bonds or ((6674aff9-00e5-47ae-990b-2da1d55c1de3))s in exchange for cash\n\t\t- In practice, central banks are always engaged in purchase and sales operations and their true quantitative monetary policy stance can be observed by netting out all their transactions\n\t\t- With ((6674a921-d46f-4adb-9b5d-a99ba47d7fa7)) and reverse repos central banks can add or substract liquidity from the financial system very quickly and precisely\n\t\t- withdrawing liquidity\n\t\t\t- The central bank sells government bonds in the [[interbank market]]\n\t\t\t  logseq.order-list-type:: number\n\t\t\t- It receives ((6665782c-8bea-467c-8657-7183e047c130)) in return, withdrawing reserves from ((66670527-36b8-48cb-a890-6c1eb573c785))s\n\t\t\t  logseq.order-list-type:: number\n\t\t- increasing liquidity\n\t\t\t- Bank of England buys government bonds to the interbank money market\n\t\t\t  logseq.order-list-type:: number\n\t\t\t- It provides ((6665782c-8bea-467c-8657-7183e047c130)) in return, increasing ((6665782c-8bea-467c-8657-7183e047c130)) at ((66670527-36b8-48cb-a890-6c1eb573c785))s thereby increasing liquidity in the system\n\t\t\t  logseq.order-list-type:: number\n\t- Standing facilities\n\t\t- Lender of last resort\n\t\t\t- The Bank of England can lend or borrow additional ((6665782c-8bea-467c-8657-7183e047c130)) to or from a ((66670527-36b8-48cb-a890-6c1eb573c785)) with a spread of 1% above and below the ((6670986e-6356-4019-b9a9-ca622bfaee13))\n\t\t\t- The Bank of England allows ((66670527-36b8-48cb-a890-6c1eb573c785))s to exchange gilts for central bank reserves overnight at a spread of 25bps  above the ((6670986e-abc1-406d-9c06-4a5cd5720586)) using the Operational Lending Facility\n\t\t\t- Asset Purchase Facility is used to apply ((667489d8-57ac-433e-aa3d-298f43c25c71))\n\t\t\t\t- Allows the central bank to purchase gilts and other types of assets outright, for which it issues newly created central bank reserves\n\t\t\t\t- This may help drive down interest rates in asset markets and increase liquidity with the intention of incentivising banks to begin lending again\n\t\t\t- Discount Window Facility\n\t\t\t\t- Allows ((66670527-36b8-48cb-a890-6c1eb573c785))s to borrow gilts from the central bank in exchange for other less liquid collateral and then excahnge these gilts for ((6665782c-8bea-467c-8657-7183e047c130)) on the [[interbank market]]\n\t- quantitative easing (QE)\n\t  id:: 667489d8-57ac-433e-aa3d-298f43c25c71\n\t\t- impact\n\t\t\t- as commercial banks hold significantly higher levels of central bank reserves, it is hoped the additional liquidity will enable them to increase their lending to the real economy, creating credit for new GDP transactions (the ‘liquidity effect’)\n\t\t\t  logseq.order-list-type:: number\n\t\t\t\t- This is however the weakest part of the argument, as in the\n\t\t\t\t  past, as evidenced by Japan’s experience, this has not been possible due to banks’ higher risk aversion,\n\t\t\t\t  triggered by large amounts of non-performing assets\n\t\t\t- Due to central bank purchases of such large quantities of government bonds, their availability in the markets decreases. It is then hoped investors will turn to other forms of investment which would support businesses (the ‘portfolio rebalancing’ effect), however, only the purchase of newly issued corporate bonds and equity in the primary market will increase purchasing power of businesses and the primary market is only a fraction of the overall turnover of capital markets.\n\t\t\t  logseq.order-list-type:: number\n\t\t\t- By purchasing gilts on such a large scale, the Bank of England hopes to push up their price and thereby push down the interest rate received by investors. Again, it is anticipated this will make other types of financial assets more attractive and stimulate growth: the ‘wealth effect’.\n\t\t\t  logseq.order-list-type:: number\n\t\t\t- All three channels are indirect, and all attempt to stimulate the real economy by acting through the financial sector. Thus bond purchase operations by central banks, including what is styled as QE, do not create new credit or deposits (purchasing power) directly in the hands of households, businesses or the Government. New credit may be created in the non-bank financial (or investment) sector. The investment sector may choose to invest this new purchasing power in newly issued corporate bonds or equity that may allow companies to increase their spending. However, it may also choose to buy government or\n\t\t\t  corporate bonds from outside the UK, or it may invest in existing financial assets such as previously issued bonds or equities, or derivatives based on commodities such as oil or food, which will have the effect of inflating the prices of these assets. Or it may simply sit on these deposits because of concerns about the future of the economy.",536897404]],["^15",[1121,"^19",1718911787932,536876418]],["^15",[1121,"^1:","~m1731870845697",536897403]],["^15",[1121,"^Z","pages/central bank.md",536876418]],["^15",[1121,"^1;",6982,536904132]],["^15",[1122,"^K",1718911787930,536876418]],["^15",[1122,"^[",1121,536876418]],["^15",[1122,"^@",false,536876418]],["^15",[1122,"^Y","central bank",536876418]],["^15",[1122,"^11","central bank",536876418]],["^15",[1122,"^?",["^ ","^17",["^18",["finance"]]],536876418]],["^15",[1122,"^4",["^ ","^17","finance"],536876418]],["^15",[1122,"^P",1101,536896361]],["^15",[1122,"^B",1731870845235,536897402]],["^15",[1122,"^;","~u67797564-b66d-4eb1-b7ac-002ac67650c9",536897852]],["^15",[1123,"^Q","tags:: finance\n\n",536876418]],["^15",[1123,"^O","^16",536876418]],["^15",[1123,"^1B",["^18",[]],536896361]],["^15",[1123,"^F",1122,536876418]],["^15",[1123,"^X",1122,536876418]],["^15",[1123,"^V",1122,536876418]],["^15",[1123,"^U",1101,536876418]],["^15",[1123,"^U",1122,536876418]],["^15",[1123,"^:",true,536896361]],["^15",[1123,"^?",["^ ","^17",["^18",["finance"]]],536896361]],["^15",[1123,"^J",["^17"],536896361]],["^15",[1123,"^4",["^ ","^17","finance"],536896361]],["^15",[1123,"^H",1101,536896361]],["^15",[1123,"^;","~u6674832b-19f8-49ca-9dea-d91933b06621",536876418]],["^15",[1124,"^Q","Implements the nation's ((667483a2-4985-4618-a070-1de207083ed8))",536876528]],["^15",[1124,"^O","^16",536876418]],["^15",[1124,"^F",1123,536876418]],["^15",[1124,"^X",1122,536876418]],["^15",[1124,"^V",1122,536876418]],["^15",[1124,"^U",1122,536876529]],["^15",[1124,"^U",1126,536876529]],["^15",[1124,"^H",1126,536896361]],["^15",[1124,"^;","~u6674832b-4464-4a3a-b668-468f35805113",536876418]],["^15",[1125,"^Q","[mergersandinquisitions.com](https://mergersandinquisitions.com)",536884346]],["^15",[1125,"^O","^16",536876424]],["^15",[1125,"^@",false,536876424]],["^15",[1125,"^F",1101,536876424]],["^15",[1125,"^X",1101,536876424]],["^15",[1125,"^V",1101,536876424]],["^15",[1125,"^U",1101,536876425]],["^15",[1125,"^;","~u66748341-cacc-4276-b97c-6a8c19815452",536876424]],["^15",[1126,"^M",false,536877908]],["^15",[1126,"^Q","monetary policy\nid:: 667483a2-4985-4618-a070-1de207083ed8",536876521]],["^15",[1126,"^O","^16",536876450]],["^15",[1126,"^F",558,536876454]],["^15",[1126,"^X",538,536876450]],["^15",[1126,"^V",538,536876454]],["^15",[1126,"^U",538,536876451]],["^15",[1126,"^?",["^ ","^1G","667483a2-4985-4618-a070-1de207083ed8"],536876521]],["^15",[1126,"^J",["^14",["^1G"]],536876521]],["^15",[1126,"^4",["^ ","^1G","667483a2-4985-4618-a070-1de207083ed8"],536876521]],["^15",[1126,"^;","~u667483a2-4985-4618-a070-1de207083ed8",536876450]],["^15",[1127,"^Q","Set of tools used by a nation's [[central bank]] to control the overall money supply and promote economic growth and employ strategies such as revising interest rates and changing bank reserve requirements",536876518]],["^15",[1127,"^O","^16",536876464]],["^15",[1127,"^F",1126,536876464]],["^15",[1127,"^X",538,536876464]],["^15",[1127,"^V",1126,536876468]],["^15",[1127,"^U",538,536876522]],["^15",[1127,"^U",1122,536876522]],["^15",[1127,"^?",["^ "],536876518]],["^15",[1127,"^H",1122,536876518]],["^15",[1127,"^;","~u667483a8-9203-4077-9205-b844727dbaf5",536876464]],["^15",[1128,"^Q","((667483a2-4985-4618-a070-1de207083ed8)) tools",536876540]],["^15",[1128,"^O","^16",536876532]],["^15",[1128,"^F",1153,536877406]],["^15",[1128,"^X",1122,536876532]],["^15",[1128,"^V",1122,536876532]],["^15",[1128,"^U",1122,536876537]],["^15",[1128,"^U",1126,536876537]],["^15",[1128,"^H",1126,536896361]],["^15",[1128,"^;","~u667489c7-802d-465d-b75e-30e5d6bf1f07",536876532]],["^15",[1129,"^Q","quantitative easing (QE)\nid:: 667489d8-57ac-433e-aa3d-298f43c25c71",536879063]],["^15",[1129,"^O","^16",536876541]],["^15",[1129,"^F",1137,536878596]],["^15",[1129,"^X",1122,536876541]],["^15",[1129,"^V",1128,536876543]],["^15",[1129,"^U",1122,536877407]],["^15",[1129,"^U",1126,536877407]],["^15",[1129,"^?",["^ ","^1G","667489d8-57ac-433e-aa3d-298f43c25c71"],536896361]],["^15",[1129,"^J",["^1G"],536896361]],["^15",[1129,"^4",["^ ","^1G","667489d8-57ac-433e-aa3d-298f43c25c71"],536896361]],["^15",[1129,"^;","~u667489d8-57ac-433e-aa3d-298f43c25c71",536876541]],["^15",[1131,"^Q","impact",536876587]],["^15",[1131,"^O","^16",536876572]],["^15",[1131,"^F",1129,536876572]],["^15",[1131,"^X",1122,536876572]],["^15",[1131,"^V",1129,536876581]],["^15",[1131,"^U",1122,536879064]],["^15",[1131,"^U",1126,536879064]],["^15",[1131,"^;","~u667489f3-8249-4b6e-88ad-9c5519e2b3a6",536876572]],["^15",[1132,"^Q","as commercial banks hold significantly higher levels of central bank reserves, it is hoped the additional liquidity will enable them to increase their lending to the real economy, creating credit for new GDP transactions (the ‘liquidity effect’)\nlogseq.order-list-type:: number",536896361]],["^15",[1132,"^O","^16",536876588]],["^15",[1132,"^F",1131,536876588]],["^15",[1132,"^X",1122,536876588]],["^15",[1132,"^V",1131,536876590]],["^15",[1132,"^U",1122,536879064]],["^15",[1132,"^U",1126,536879064]],["^15",[1132,"^?",["^ ","~:logseq.order-list-type","number"],536896361]],["^15",[1132,"^J",["^1H"],536896361]],["^15",[1132,"^4",["^ ","^1H","number"],536896361]],["^15",[1132,"^;","~u66748a03-6820-4efc-8940-7b3d06f6e9f0",536876588]],["^15",[1133,"^Q","This is however the weakest part of the argument, as in the\npast, as evidenced by Japan’s experience, this has not been possible due to banks’ higher risk aversion,\ntriggered by large amounts of non-performing assets",536876613]],["^15",[1133,"^O","^16",536876606]],["^15",[1133,"^F",1132,536876606]],["^15",[1133,"^X",1122,536876606]],["^15",[1133,"^V",1132,536876610]],["^15",[1133,"^U",1122,536879064]],["^15",[1133,"^U",1126,536879064]],["^15",[1133,"^;","~u66748a24-1eaf-4487-ab74-559d659429a2",536876606]],["^15",[1136,"^Q","All three channels are indirect, and all attempt to stimulate the real economy by acting through the financial sector. Thus bond purchase operations by central banks, including what is styled as QE, do not create new credit or deposits (purchasing power) directly in the hands of households, businesses or the Government. New credit may be created in the non-bank financial (or investment) sector. The investment sector may choose to invest this new purchasing power in newly issued corporate bonds or equity that may allow companies to increase their spending. However, it may also choose to buy government or\ncorporate bonds from outside the UK, or it may invest in existing financial assets such as previously issued bonds or equities, or derivatives based on commodities such as oil or food, which will have the effect of inflating the prices of these assets. Or it may simply sit on these deposits because of concerns about the future of the economy.",536876740]],["^15",[1136,"^O","^16",536876686]],["^15",[1136,"^F",1201,536878082]],["^15",[1136,"^X",1122,536876686]],["^15",[1136,"^V",1131,536876686]],["^15",[1136,"^U",1122,536879064]],["^15",[1136,"^U",1126,536879064]],["^15",[1136,"^;","~u66748b2a-93af-4b87-8c20-2922eb3068df",536876686]],["^15",[1137,"^Q","Standing facilities",536878581]],["^15",[1137,"^O","^16",536876743]],["^15",[1137,"^F",1138,536878588]],["^15",[1137,"^X",1122,536876743]],["^15",[1137,"^V",1128,536878588]],["^15",[1137,"^U",1122,536878585]],["^15",[1137,"^U",1126,536878585]],["^15",[1137,"^;","~u66748d44-720c-4f06-980b-2645b63f0a97",536876743]],["^15",[1138,"^Q","Open Market Operations (OMO)",536876769]],["^15",[1138,"^O","^16",536876759]],["^15",[1138,"^F",1128,536878584]],["^15",[1138,"^X",1122,536876759]],["^15",[1138,"^V",1128,536876759]],["^15",[1138,"^U",1122,536877407]],["^15",[1138,"^U",1126,536877407]],["^15",[1138,"^;","~u66748d54-1352-4cd4-979d-af1f06edb695",536876759]],["^15",[1139,"^Q","Rather than try to regulate the quantity of credit it attempts to influence the **price of credit** using its monetary policy tools",536876888]],["^15",[1139,"^O","^16",536876772]],["^15",[1139,"^F",1124,536876772]],["^15",[1139,"^X",1122,536876772]],["^15",[1139,"^V",1124,536876776]],["^15",[1139,"^U",1122,536876824]],["^15",[1139,"^U",1126,536876824]],["^15",[1139,"^;","~u66748e8c-68a0-40d8-8966-b6b2c06bcde8",536876772]],["^15",[1142,"^Q","Every commercial bank may need to borrow reserves from either the central bank or other commercial banks",536876925]],["^15",[1142,"^O","^16",536876888]],["^15",[1142,"^F",1139,536876888]],["^15",[1142,"^X",1122,536876888]],["^15",[1142,"^V",1124,536876888]],["^15",[1142,"^U",1122,536876889]],["^15",[1142,"^U",1126,536876889]],["^15",[1142,"^;","~u667490b9-7dc9-47fc-8dad-aa7f72ab8bd6",536876888]],["^15",[1143,"^Q","Banks access reserves indirectly via the interbank or wholesale market by selling or lending government securities (gilts)",536876983]],["^15",[1143,"^O","^16",536876928]],["^15",[1143,"^F",1142,536876928]],["^15",[1143,"^X",1122,536876928]],["^15",[1143,"^V",1124,536876935]],["^15",[1143,"^U",1122,536876929]],["^15",[1143,"^U",1126,536876929]],["^15",[1143,"^;","~u667490f5-a344-40df-97d8-8cc28b425a3c",536876928]],["^15",[1144,"^Q","Banks lend reserves to each other at the market rate of interest. The closer the market rate of interest is to the ((6670986e-abc1-406d-9c06-4a5cd5720586)) the more effectively changes in the ((6670986e-abc1-406d-9c06-4a5cd5720586)) will carry through and the more reliably monetary policy is implemented",536877445]],["^15",[1144,"^O","^16",536876983]],["^15",[1144,"^F",1143,536876983]],["^15",[1144,"^X",1122,536876983]],["^15",[1144,"^V",1124,536876983]],["^15",[1144,"^U",1122,536877446]],["^15",[1144,"^U",1126,536877446]],["^15",[1144,"^U",1174,536877446]],["^15",[1144,"^H",1174,536896361]],["^15",[1144,"^;","~u66749140-6c69-458e-b295-ade3c8bf7ecc",536876983]],["^15",[1146,"^Q","The central bank cannot directly determine the market rate of interest in the interbank market, but it can affect the market rate of interest by lending and borrowing reserves itself on this market to try and keep this rate close to the policy rate. These loans are conducted via repurchasing agreements (repos) and other open-market operations or through providing ‘standing facilities’.",536877101]],["^15",[1146,"^O","^16",536877081]],["^15",[1146,"^F",1144,536877081]],["^15",[1146,"^X",1122,536877081]],["^15",[1146,"^V",1124,536877081]],["^15",[1146,"^U",1122,536877082]],["^15",[1146,"^U",1126,536877082]],["^15",[1146,"^;","~u667491fd-9b81-4314-8374-c60a17be2a5a",536877081]],["^15",[1153,"^Q","Banks are required to hold a certain amount of ((6665782c-8bea-467c-8657-7183e047c130)) with the central bank",536877410]],["^15",[1153,"^O","^16",536877398]],["^15",[1153,"^F",1124,536877406]],["^15",[1153,"^X",1122,536877398]],["^15",[1153,"^V",1122,536877406]],["^15",[1153,"^U",707,536877411]],["^15",[1153,"^U",1122,536877411]],["^15",[1153,"^H",707,536896361]],["^15",[1153,"^;","~u6670986e-8aa9-43d8-9738-2db2b73efbdb",536877410]],["^15",[1154,"^Q","TODO define what this \"certain amount\" is",536877410]],["^15",[1154,"^O","^16",536877410]],["^15",[1154,"^F",1153,536877410]],["^15",[1154,"^10","TODO",536896361]],["^15",[1154,"^X",1122,536877410]],["^15",[1154,"^V",1153,536877410]],["^15",[1154,"^U",4,536877411]],["^15",[1154,"^U",672,536877411]],["^15",[1154,"^U",707,536877411]],["^15",[1154,"^U",1122,536877411]],["^15",[1154,"^H",4,536896361]],["^15",[1154,"^;","~u6674947e-29a7-45dc-aaf5-0facbed78690",536877410]],["^15",[1155,"^Q","Financial institutions may have a surplus or deficit of ((6665782c-8bea-467c-8657-7183e047c130)) so they borrow and lend to each other in this market",536877410]],["^15",[1155,"^O","^16",536877410]],["^15",[1155,"^F",1154,536877410]],["^15",[1155,"^X",1122,536877410]],["^15",[1155,"^V",1153,536877410]],["^15",[1155,"^U",672,536877411]],["^15",[1155,"^U",707,536877411]],["^15",[1155,"^U",1122,536877411]],["^15",[1155,"^H",707,536896361]],["^15",[1155,"^;","~u6670986e-4842-4569-a6f9-3774ddf7ea6f",536877410]],["^15",[1156,"^Q","The majority of these loans are made overnight it is also know as the overnight market",536877410]],["^15",[1156,"^O","^16",536877410]],["^15",[1156,"^F",1155,536877410]],["^15",[1156,"^X",1122,536877410]],["^15",[1156,"^V",1153,536877410]],["^15",[1156,"^U",672,536877411]],["^15",[1156,"^U",707,536877411]],["^15",[1156,"^U",1122,536877411]],["^15",[1156,"^;","~u667493ae-63da-409c-9faf-3049c5a73d57",536877410]],["^15",[1157,"^Q","The central bank sells government bonds in the [[interbank market]]\nlogseq.order-list-type:: number",536897402]],["^15",[1157,"^O","^16",536877414]],["^15",[1157,"^F",1204,536878109]],["^15",[1157,"^X",1122,536877414]],["^15",[1157,"^V",1204,536878131]],["^15",[1157,"^U",1122,536878585]],["^15",[1157,"^U",1126,536878585]],["^15",[1157,"^U",1158,536878585]],["^15",[1157,"^?",["^ ","^1H","number"],536897402]],["^15",[1157,"^J",["^14",["^1H"]],536897402]],["^15",[1157,"^4",["^ ","^1H","number"],536897402]],["^15",[1157,"^H",1158,536897402]],["^15",[1157,"^;","~u66749a36-68b5-4f0a-a98e-32e3c101726f",536877414]],["^15",[1158,"^5",1160,536897419]],["^15",[1158,"^K",1718917788512,536877425]],["^15",[1158,"^[",1162,536877433]],["^15",[1158,"^O","^16",536877425]],["^15",[1158,"^@",false,536877425]],["^15",[1158,"^Y","interbank market",536877425]],["^15",[1158,"^11","interbank market",536877425]],["^15",[1158,"^?",["^ ","~:alias",["^18",["wholesale market"]],"^17",["^18",["finance"]]],536897419]],["^15",[1158,"^4",["^ ","^1I","wholesale market","^17","finance"],536897419]],["^15",[1158,"^P",1101,536897419]],["^15",[1158,"^B",1731870868152,536897419]],["^15",[1158,"^;","~u66fc6de7-eb73-4c91-b1ab-b89e91916597",536896361]],["^15",[1159,"^Q","alias:: wholesale market\ntags:: finance",536897419]],["^15",[1159,"^O","^16",536877426]],["^15",[1159,"^1B",["^18",[]],536897419]],["^15",[1159,"^@",false,536877426]],["^15",[1159,"^F",1158,536877426]],["^15",[1159,"^X",1158,536877426]],["^15",[1159,"^V",1158,536877426]],["^15",[1159,"^U",1101,536897420]],["^15",[1159,"^U",1158,536897420]],["^15",[1159,"^U",1160,536897420]],["^15",[1159,"^:",true,536897419]],["^15",[1159,"^?",["^ ","^1I",["^18",["wholesale market"]],"^17",["^18",["finance"]]],536897419]],["^15",[1159,"^J",["^14",["^1I","^17"]],536897419]],["^15",[1159,"^4",["^ ","^1I","wholesale market","^17","finance"],536897419]],["^15",[1159,"^H",1101,536897419]],["^15",[1159,"^H",1160,536897419]],["^15",[1159,"^;","~u66749a9c-c02c-494a-a12d-33dd2873dd18",536877426]],["^15",[1160,"^K",1718917806160,536877429]],["^15",[1160,"^@",false,536877429]],["^15",[1160,"^Y","wholesale market",536877429]],["^15",[1160,"^11","wholesale market",536877429]],["^15",[1160,"^B",1718917806160,536877429]],["^15",[1160,"^;","~u67797564-c440-46db-a343-827ee1ee6145",536897852]],["^15",[1162,"^3","alias:: wholesale market\ntags:: finance\n\n- Where financial institutions and the [[central bank]] can lend funds to each other\n- The majority of the loans are made overnight in the ((66749c89-7161-47f0-8155-5092e92a68c4))\n- overnight market\n  id:: 66749c89-7161-47f0-8155-5092e92a68c4\n\t- Participants: ((66749db0-fe3a-40d0-9d39-fbed0fd07ff6)) (mainly ((66670527-36b8-48cb-a890-6c1eb573c785))s and savings associations) and the [[central bank]]\n\t- Only short term loans (overnight or up to a few days)\n\t- Most of its activity takes place immediately after the start of business for the day\n\t- Participants forecast their client' liquidity needs for the day and either borrow or lend money from other participants\n\t- overnight rate\n\t  id:: 6670986e-b101-4237-9f74-948bf03eb201\n\t\t- Actual rate that ((66670527-36b8-48cb-a890-6c1eb573c785))s borrow and lend money to each other overnight\n\t\t- Shortest (and therefore lowest) rate\n\t\t- Each country has its own system to calculate this rate\n\t\t\t- US: effective federal funds rate\n\t\t\t- UK: Sterling Overnight Index Average (SONIA)\n\t\t\t- Eurozone: Euro Short-term rate (ESTER)\n- target overnight rate (policy rate)\n  id:: 6670986e-6356-4019-b9a9-ca622bfaee13\n\t- Target rate set by the central bank at which ((66670527-36b8-48cb-a890-6c1eb573c785))s lend and borrow their ((6665782c-8bea-467c-8657-7183e047c130))\n\t- \"Federal funds rate” in the US\n- bank rate\n  id:: 6670986e-abc1-406d-9c06-4a5cd5720586\n\t- Rate that ((66670527-36b8-48cb-a890-6c1eb573c785))s can borrow from the central bank\n\t- Effectively the cap at which the central bank will step in and lend to banks itself\n- Open Market Operations\n\t- TODO Complete this section with https://www.investopedia.com/terms/o/openmarketoperations.asp and https://economics.stackexchange.com/questions/14697/whats-the-difference-between-quantitative-easing-and-regular-central-bank-opera\n\t- Carried out by the central bank to keep the overnight rate at its target\n\t- These operations can\n\t\t- Inject money into the money supply by purchasing securities\n\t\t- Take money out of circulation by selling securities\n\t- types\n\t\t- permanent\n\t\t- temporary",536897422]],["^15",[1162,"^1:","~m1731870868829",536897421]],["^15",[1162,"^Z","pages/interbank market.md",536877433]],["^15",[1162,"^1;",2131,536904132]],["^15",[1163,"^Q","Where financial institutions and the [[central bank]] can lend funds to each other",536877736]],["^15",[1163,"^O","^16",536877445]],["^15",[1163,"^F",1159,536897410]],["^15",[1163,"^X",1158,536877445]],["^15",[1163,"^V",1158,536877458]],["^15",[1163,"^U",1122,536877452]],["^15",[1163,"^U",1158,536877452]],["^15",[1163,"^?",["^ "],536897410]],["^15",[1163,"^H",1122,536897410]],["^15",[1163,"^;","~u66749583-9a74-471d-9bfc-41e1751b2493",536877445]],["^15",[1165,"^Q","target overnight rate (policy rate)\nid:: 6670986e-6356-4019-b9a9-ca622bfaee13",536878791]],["^15",[1165,"^O","^16",536877445]],["^15",[1165,"^F",1188,536877553]],["^15",[1165,"^X",1158,536877445]],["^15",[1165,"^V",1158,536877458]],["^15",[1165,"^U",1158,536877452]],["^15",[1165,"^?",["^ ","^1G","6670986e-6356-4019-b9a9-ca622bfaee13"],536878791]],["^15",[1165,"^J",["^14",["^1G"]],536878791]],["^15",[1165,"^4",["^ ","^1G","6670986e-6356-4019-b9a9-ca622bfaee13"],536878791]],["^15",[1165,"^